<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sharur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1501">1501</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sharur was fought in 1501 in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, where Ismail, head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safaviyya">Safaviyya order</a>, led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qizilbash">Qizilbash</a> to victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> confederation. Ismail then seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and declared himself Shah of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. The battle is regarded as the founding event of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sharur.jpg" alt="Battle of Sharur" width="320" height="552" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist, c. 1590–1600 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Negotiations_between_Alwand_and_Ismail,_followed_by_the_battle_of_Sharur_(1501)._Habib_al-siyar,_end_of_16th_century._National_Palace_Museum_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
